    "body": "## Problem\n\n`g@<C-v>j` and `y<C-v>j` set `']` one character short of the block, so 'operatorfunc' cannot see the block. A linewise motion forced blockwise stayed non-inclusive, and `decl()` backed the end mark up. On column 1 that lands on the previous line. On a short last line with `'virtualedit'` \"block\", the right edge is lost and the yank is one column narrow.\n\n## Solution\n\n`get_op_vcol()` set `motion_type` to blockwise before `do_pending_operator()` decided `inclusive`. Vim keeps the block in `block_mode` and leaves `motion_type` as `MLINE` until after that check, so a linewise motion is inclusive.\n\nDecide `inclusive` from the motion's own type, then mark the operation blockwise.\n\n## Test\n\n`TEST_FILE=test/functional/editor/operator_spec.lua make functionaltest`\n\nThe new test covers `<C-v>j`, `<C-v>e`, and a short line with `virtualedit=block`, for both `g@` and `y`. It also checks that `d<C-v>j` and a visual-block delete still remove only the block.\n\nFixes neovim/neovim#42309",
    "closed_at": null,
