            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Small suggestion: this comment explains a line that is not there anymore. A new reader does not know that `motion_type` was set here before, so \"stays\" is hard to understand. `kMTBlockWise` is now set next to the `'V'` and `'v'` cases, and the test covers the order, so I think the comment can go.\n\n```suggestion\n```",
            "commit_id": "c8b373de9ec069137affad70524c38420c3a47a0",
            "created_at": "2026-10-12T17:35:04Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -3352,7 +3352,9 @@ static void get_op_vcol(oparg_T *oap, bool initial)\n     return;\n   }\n \n-  oap->motion_type = kMTBlockWise;\n+  // motion_type stays the motion's own type. do_pending_operator() uses it to\n+  // decide \"inclusive\" (a linewise motion forced blockwise is inclusive), then\n+  // sets kMTBlockWise.",
