    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks for this PR. It fixes the linewise case (`<C-v>j`). But the exclusive case (row 3 in #42309) is not fixed:\r\n\r\n```\r\n:call setline(1, ['ab cd'])\r\n0y<C-v>w\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe register is correct (`ab c`). But `']` is at column 3. It must be at column 4. With `selection=exclusive`, `02|y<C-v>l` puts `']` before `'[`.\r\n\r\nThe cause: `op_function()` and `op_yank_reg()` do `decl()` on blocks too. For a block, `oap->end` is already the last column.\r\n\r\nI have a fix with a test: https://github.com/Nagato-Yuzuru/neovim/commit/c4592655339c6d43b799f1f5b65f2f4fe912fedb\r\n\r\nIt changes only these two conditions. It applies cleanly on this branch:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ngit fetch https://github.com/Nagato-Yuzuru/neovim fix-forced-block-exclusive\r\ngit cherry-pick c4592655339c\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou can add it to this PR. Or I can send a separate PR after this PR is merged.",
            "created_at": "2026-10-12T17:26:52Z",
